```c
// Global shared variable
int counter = 0;

void increment_counter() {
    // This is the critical section
    int temp = counter; // Read 'counter'
    temp = temp + 1;    // Modify 'temp'
    counter = temp;     // Write 'temp' back to 'counter'
}
```
The race occurs because the read, modify, and write operations on `counter` are not atomic; another thread can interleave its operations between them.
